/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the angle with a measure $90^\\circ$ on our diagram.\n\n![](images/85/859dda507ff6f983a091ecdbf62e01d27230bb210626232388fd344c3e194a8c.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the angle $\\angle{COD}$ (or $\\angle{DOC}$) has a measure of $90^\\circ.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133465 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10600" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133465 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f0/f00f3f66717f230fb42264ca5a0873b394ea1d86002f00517062287f8983f236.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of the angle $\\angle{NRP}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5df19497-b07f-57e3-9589-a488291147bf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133465 #edb/ref 1074 "If we trace along the letters of the angle name, from $N$ to $R$ to $P,$ we can see the angle $\\angle{NRP}.$\n\n![](images/1a/1a9498bf166c686b8c2e5c3017aeb8625cf36c35d20069f5eb82adcc5c797fa8.png)\n\nTherefore, $m\\angle{NRP}=110^\\circ.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133540 #edb/ref 1069 "e-2584" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133540 #edb/ref 1071 "Which numbered angle refers to the same angle as $\\widehat{GHA}?$\n\n![](images/47/47841a386b57f8615897cb73b1b98f15e975c78722f29d8baca92e7c7663a527.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133540 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebc8ba04-2c55-56bd-b07c-f5f95d0841c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133540 #edb/ref 1074 "If we trace along the letters of the angle name, from $G$ to $H$ to $A$,  we see that $\\widehat{GHA}$ refers to the angle $\\angle 3.$\n\n![](images/10/100349e33233f2152ce236be2d17dc2fe3a59035a88336e26554eb6864d6059a.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\angle{3}$ is another name for $\\widehat{GHA}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133909 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133909 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133909 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133909 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186430905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186